// =============================================================================
// std/builtin/type_aliases.code — Types that name something about types
// =============================================================================
//
// These are built-ins in the sense that the prelude re-exports them, so no
// module has to import them.
// =============================================================================

// A type that can never have an instance constructed, used as the result of
// a function that never returns.
//
// This is an ordinary enum with no variants: it is genuinely impossible to
// construct, which is the property callers rely on when they write
// `-> Never`. What the compiler does not yet do is *use* that fact -- it
// draws no conclusion about the code following such a call being
// unreachable. The inference is the part still missing, not the type.
public enum Never {}
